// Class: TSSHOCK family (Verichains 2022 α-shuffle; Thorchain 2026 c-split).
// Root cause: Honest parties skip verification that other party's Paillier
// modulus N is product of TWO safe primes (biprime). Adversary submits
// N = p*q*r (three primes) → adversary later able to compute discrete log
// in subgroup, extract shares from MtA round.
//
// Expected outcome if BUG present:
//   1. Keygen completes without error for all parties.
//   2. After signing 1-2 messages, adversary recovers victim's secret share.
//   3. Adversary can construct valid signatures alone after share extraction.
//
// Expected outcome if BUG absent (correctly patched):
//   1. Honest parties REJECT adversary's keygen round 1 contribution.
//   2. Keygen aborts with an error such as "paillier key not biprime".

